// Jalandhar drops the "low-growth paths" row (index 2) and the "random
// upskilling" row (index 5). Index 2 is the weakest fit here - a working
// sports-goods export unit and an IELTS-versus-build-in-India decision are not
// a "low-growth path" narrative, they are specific, concrete forks the page's
// own local sections already carry. Index 5 is dropped for the same reason it
// is dropped on Chennai: the page's forks are named and specific (IELTS/abroad,
// family export business, LPU-corridor stay-or-return), not the vague "random
// upskilling" the row describes. The resulting selection (rows 0, 1, 3, 4) is a
// combination not used by any sibling: Rajkot (rows 0-4), Vizag (rows 1-5),
// Bangalore (full library), Pune (drops index 3), Kolkata (drops index 1),
// Chennai (drops index 5 only), Hyderabad (drops index 2 only), Mumbai/
// Chandigarh/Gurgaon/Nagpur (drop index 4 only), Delhi (drops 0 and 5),
// Ahmedabad (drops 3 and 5), Surat (drops 0 and 3), Ludhiana (drops 1 and 4),
// Thane (drops 1 and 3), and Guwahati (drops 2 and 4).
